  "question": "Masses of $1$ kg, $2$ kg and $3$ kg are placed at the points $(0, 0)$, $(2, 0)$ and $(0, 2)$ m respectively. The position of their centre of mass is",
  "diagram": "",
  "diagram_alt": "",
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$(1,\\ 1)$ m",
      "image": ""
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\left(1,\\ \\dfrac{2}{3}\\right)$ m",
      "image": ""
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\left(\\dfrac{2}{3},\\ \\dfrac{2}{3}\\right)$ m",
      "image": ""
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\left(\\dfrac{2}{3},\\ 1\\right)$ m",
      "image": ""
    }
  ],
  "answer": "D",
  "numerical_answer": "",
  "tolerance": "",
  "solution": "$$x_{cm} = \\frac{1(0) + 2(2) + 3(0)}{6} = \\frac{2}{3}\\ \\text{m}, \\qquad y_{cm} = \\frac{1(0) + 2(0) + 3(2)}{6} = 1\\ \\text{m}$$",
